{title: 062 - How Lovely Is Thy Dwelling Place}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]How love[F]ly [Bb]is Thy [Ab]dwelling [Eb]place,
[F]O [Eb]Lord [Bb]of [Cm7]hosts [F7]to [Bb]me![Cm][Bb]
[Dm7]The [Gm]tabe[Cm7]nacles [F]of [F7]Thy [Bb]grace
[Eb]How [Dm]pleasant, [Cm7]Lord, [F7]they [Bb]be!

Verse 2:
[Bb]My [F]thirsty [Bb]soul [Ab]longs [Eb]ardently,
[F][Eb]Yea, [Bb]faints [Cm7]Thy [F7][Bb]courts [Cm]to [Bb]see;
[Dm7]My [Gm]very [Cm7]heart [F]and [F7]flesh [Bb]cry out,
[Eb]O [Dm]living [Cm7]God, [F7]for [Bb]Thee.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Behold [F]the [Bb]sparrow [Ab]findeth [Eb]out
[F][Eb]A [Bb][Cm7]house [F7]where-in [Bb][Cm]to [Bb]rest;
[Dm7][Gm]The [Cm7]swallow [F]also, [F7]for [Bb]herself
[Eb][Dm]Provided [Cm7]hath [F7]a [Bb]nest.

Verse 4:
[Bb]Ev'n [F]Thine [Bb]own altars, [Ab]where [Eb]she safe
[F][Eb]Her [Bb]young [Cm7]ones [F7][Bb]forth [Cm]may [Bb]bring,
[Dm7]O [Gm]Thou, [Cm7]almighty [F]Lord [F7]of [Bb]hosts,
[Eb]Who [Dm]art [Cm7]my [F7]God [Bb]and King.

Verse 5:
[Bb]Blest [F]are they [Bb]in [Ab]Thy house [Eb]that dwell,
[F][Eb]They [Bb][Cm7]ever [F7]give [Bb][Cm]Thee [Bb]praise.
[Dm7]Blest [Gm]is [Cm7]the man [F]whose [F7]strength [Bb]Thou art,
[Eb]In [Dm]whose [Cm7]heart [F7]are [Bb]Thy ways.
